# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Agent skill folders and local Claude Code state. Skills are installed per
# user, not vendored here: a copy is symlinked, which breaks on Windows.
.agents/
.claude/

# Scratch. Drafts and working notes a skill writes on the way to a real
# artifact: a ticket body before it is filed, a spec before it is published.
# Never an input to anything, so nothing is lost by ignoring it. Listed
# because the directory is otherwise untracked-but-unignored, which is one
# `git add -A` away from committing a draft to a public repository.
.scratch/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Data — CMUdict, prevalence norms and derived indexes are large and
# regenerable. See docs/adr/0003 and docs/adr/0004. The committed pronunciation
# supplement (ADR-0009) is the one hand-authored input, so it is kept.
/data/*
!/data/supplement.dict
# The schedule is dealt once, reviewed by hand and then fixed (ADR-0012), so it
# is an authored input like the supplement — not a regenerable artifact.
!/data/schedule.json
# The demotion list corrects the upstream word list's proper nouns and junk
# (ADR-0011, amended). Hand-authored, so it is kept for the same reason.
!/data/demotions.txt
# The editor's standing rulings over the Candidate Queue (#176, ADR-0017). Kept
# for the demotion list's reason and one more: it is the only record that a
# Candidate was ever considered and rejected. Nothing derives it — resolution is
# derived, a Decline is the one thing written — so a copy on one machine would
# lose every ruling the next clone made again.
!/data/declines.txt
# The Unconfirmed Rhymes the Judge writes (#259, ADR-0017). Authored, like the
# demotion list, so kept for its reason: the next clone could not derive it.
!/data/unconfirmed-rhymes.txt
# The Editor's Pass defers what it cannot compose a reading for. Unlike the
# Appeal candidates queue beside it, which is pulled down from R2 and can be
# pulled again, this is the only record that a miss happened — it is the work
# list for a later pass and the instrument that turns "7 out of 7" into a real
# miss rate (ADR-0014). A record kept on one machine measures nothing.
!/data/deferred-readings.jsonl
# The four large sources are not committed: they are mirrored in private R2
# and pinned by checksum (#272, ADR-0013 amended). The checksums are committed
# so the laptop and CI build from the same bytes, and the provenance record the
# index serialises is committed so a fresh clone can build at all.
!/data/sources.sha256
!/data/sources.json
*.csv
*.xlsx
# The Retrieval override layer, and the one negation that has to come after the
# blanket `*.csv` above rather than beside its neighbours: git applies these in
# order, so `!/data/tier-overrides.csv` placed with the others would be
# re-ignored two lines later. It is exempted for the strongest reason on this
# list — ADR-0015 records that it can never be regenerated. Every other data
# file here is either derived from a pinned source or reconstructible by hand;
# a Tier verdict is a judgement about Retrieval that only the editor who made it
# holds, and `*.csv` was quietly making a night of them uncommittable.
!/data/tier-overrides.csv
# The maintainer's verdicts the Judge is scored against, authored like the
# demotion list, and the report every Judge and Synthetic Player run commits
# (#250). Neither can be regenerated: one is a person's ear, the other a record
# of what a model said on a day.
!/data/judge-labels/
!/data/judge-runs/
# Every Candidate the Judge has ruled on and what landed (#266). It is what keeps
# a Candidate from being sent twice, and where the Editor's Pass reads the
# Judge's ruling from, so a fresh clone without it would re-draw every ruling.
!/data/judge-rulings.jsonl
# Raw model output from those runs, kept only so an interrupted run resumes
# rather than pays twice. Not in .scratch/, which is for drafts.
.model-cache/
# Docs
deploy_walkthrough.md
# Dependencies / build
node_modules/
dist/
dist-data/
build/
.env
.env.local

# Cloudflare deploy credentials — the read-only R2 token the Appeal pull
# script uses (#114). Local only; the Worker's own secrets live on the Worker,
# never in the repo.
credentials.env

